"epic picture" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-picture&gt;
		<header>The &lt;epic-picture&gt; element: a picture the person gave an item, a thumbnail with a trash that deletes it and its file.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>A picture you paste into the chat while asking for a fix goes onto the issue or todo it becomes. <text code>&lt;epic-picture&gt;</> shows it in the item, after your words: a thumbnail, which a click opens full size.</>
	<text paragraph>Each picture has a label, IMG1, IMG2 and so on, in a small chip on its top left corner. Write "IMG2 is wrong" in a comment or a note, and Claude knows which file you mean. Every place on a page that takes pictures draws them this way: a comment, a note, an option's form, a new epic's kickoff box.</>
	<text paragraph>On an epic page being reviewed, a trash sits at its top right corner. One click deletes it: it goes at once, with Undo in the page's notices for 6 seconds; then the page server takes it out of the item and deletes its file.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>
		For anyone reviewing an epic page.

		Status: <label size="mini" color="green">built</> (epic <text code>epic-engine</> T87, labelled in P75), its own <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-picture" link="/epic/src/components/epic-picture/"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-picture/" code>epic-picture</></> family.

		Its vocabulary: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-picture-epicpicture-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-picture/EpicPicture.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-picture/EpicPicture.en.ts" code>EpicPicture.en.ts</></>

		Its component: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-picture-epicpicture-tsx" link="/epic/src/components/epic-picture/EpicPicture.tsx"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-picture/EpicPicture.tsx" code>EpicPicture.tsx</></>.
	</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<text paragraph>An issue filed with a picture pasted in the chat. The trash shows only on an epic page being reviewed: here, the picture alone.</>
		<html>
			<ui-stack>
				<epic-section id="issues" kind="issues" open>
					<epic-item id="i9" title="The popup covers its button" status="open">
						<p>Owen: “the popup covers the button, see the picture”</>
						<epic-picture label="IMG1">
							<img src="/components/ui/images/new_popup_alignment.png" alt="Picture pasted in the chat" />
						</>
					</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
		<text paragraph>The item above:</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<epic-item id="i9" title="The popup covers its button" status="open">
			  <p>Owen: “the popup covers the button, see the picture”</p>
			  <epic-picture label="IMG1"><img src="pictures/i9-20261116-1302.png" alt="Picture pasted in the chat" /></epic-picture>
			</epic-item>
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Behaviour">
		<icon slot="icon" name="hand pointer"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Its picture is the <text code>&lt;img&gt;</> inside it: a page with no script shows it too.</>
			<item>A thumbnail, at most 320px wide and 240px tall, its shape kept; a click opens it full size.</>
			<item>Its item is the <text code>&lt;epic-item&gt;</> it's written in.</>
			<item>Not reviewed: no trash.</>
			<item>The trash: one click, no dialog, as a comment's. The picture hides at once; "Picture deleted" shows with Undo for 6 seconds.</>
			<item>Then the page server takes it out of the item, writes a line in the Log, and deletes its file. Leaving the page sooner sends the delete at once.</>
			<item>Undo puts it back, and nothing changes on disk.</>
			<item>Deleting one renumbers nothing: after IMG2 goes, the next one is still IMG3, so what was said about IMG3 stays true.</>
			<item>In a box still being written (a note, the kickoff box, an option's form), an x takes the trash's place. It takes the picture's words out of the box, and the later labels move down one, in the words that name them too: IMG3 becomes IMG2.</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>The epic tool writes it: <text code>epic add &lt;epic&gt;#I "..." --picture &lt;file&gt;</> (repeatable), and <text code>--pasted &lt;n&gt;</>, the pictures pasted last into the session's chat.</>
			<item>The files go beside the page, in <text code>pictures/</>, named for the item and the minute: <text code>pictures/i9-20261116-1302.png</>.</>
			<item>It holds one <text code>&lt;img src alt&gt;</>.</>
			<item><text code>label</>: its label, <text code>IMG2</>, written by the epic tool in the item's order.</>
			<item><text code>removable</>: an x in place of the trash, for a box still being written; its <text code>epic-picture-removed</> event hands the box its label.</>
		</>

		<section label="Parts" sticky="stack" collapsible dividing open="false">
			<table celled padding="compact" appearance="striped" unstackable>
				<row header>
					<cell>Name</>
					<cell>What it is</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>base</>
					</>
					<cell>The box around the picture.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>delete</>
					</>
					<cell>The trash, at its top right corner, while the page is reviewed.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>label</>
					</>
					<cell>Its label's chip, at its top left corner.</>
				</>
				<row>
					<cell>
						<text code>remove</>
					</>
					<cell>The x, at its top right corner, when <text code>removable</>.</>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>
	<html>
		<footer class="site-page-footer">
			<ui-divider></>
			<ui-text class="meta" paragraph>Last checked 2026-11-17 against branch <ui-text code>epic-engine</> (T87, P75).</>
		</>
	</>
